# pacman runs these as root, so they can't set Auren up for you: that's `auren setup`, which runs
# the first time you run `auren`. They only say what to do (Arch never enables user services for you).

post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Auren is installed. Set it up for yourself (as you, not root) by running:

    auren

It asks a few questions, then adds the talk keys and the bar plugin, downloads the voice model and
starts Auren. Run `auren setup` again any time.

Installed Auren with install.sh before? Run `/usr/bin/auren setup` instead: until it replaces that
copy, your old `auren` comes first in PATH. Your settings, keys and voice model are kept.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Auren was updated. Restart it when it's idle, to run the new version:

    systemctl --user try-restart auren auren-mascot

If the bar panel still looks the same, restart the bar too: omarchy restart shell
(Updating from Auren's bar panel does both for you.)
EOF
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Removing Auren. Best done after `auren setup --remove`, which takes out the talk keys, the bar plugin
and the services for your user. If you didn't, see the steps printed after removal.
EOF
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Auren has been removed. If you didn't run `auren setup --remove` first, clean up as yourself:

    systemctl --user stop auren auren-mascot
    rm -f ~/.config/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants/auren.service \
          ~/.config/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants/auren-mascot.service
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    omarchy plugin disable kvm404.auren; rm -f ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/kvm404.auren

and take the "Auren: talk" lines out of ~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua. Your settings and API key
(~/.config/auren), history (~/.local/state/auren) and voice model (~/.local/share/auren) are left
alone: delete those folders too to remove everything.
EOF
}
